[38;5;231m●[39m Implementation is complete and green. Summary of what's in place while the review agent finishes:

  [1m[38;5;153msrc/orchestrator.ts[0m (new) — the prompt text plus the resume marker.
  - [38;5;153morchestratorSystemPrompt(selfCmd)[39m takes the launcher's [38;5;153mSELF_CMD[39m as a parameter (keeps the module free of spawn-time env sniffing, and directly unit-testable).
  - I chose [38;5;153m--append-system-prompt[39m over [38;5;153m--agent[39m: [38;5;153mclaude --agent <name>[39m needs a definition on disk in the target repo, and orchestrators get launched into arbitrary repos, so the instructions
  would silently vanish where no [38;5;153m.claude/agents/orchestrator.md[39m exists. (This repo's [38;5;153m.claude/agents/[39m is in fact empty — the [38;5;153morchestrator[39m definition lives at user level in
  [38;5;153m~/.claude/agents/orchestrator.md[39m, so I reused its content rather than depending on the file.) Neither flag is recorded in claude's session state, and re-appending a system prompt on resume
  is already the codebase's proven path ([38;5;153mresumeArgv[39m).
  - Resume survival: launched ids are recorded in [38;5;153m~/.agendo/orchestrators.json[39m, and [38;5;153mresumeArgv[39m consults it — so cold resume and restore-tab replay both re-inject.

  [1mWiring[0m — [38;5;153mlaunch.ts[39m combines the launcher prompt and the orchestrator prompt into [1mone[0m [38;5;153m--append-system-prompt[39m value (claude's flag takes a single value; passing it twice would silently
  discard one). [38;5;153mLaunchOptions.orchestrator[39m threads through [38;5;153mlaunchTask[39m/[38;5;153mlaunchNewSession[39m. The worktree slug defaults to [38;5;153morchestrator[39m rather than a slug of the goal.

  [1mCLI[0m — [38;5;153magendo launch --orchestrator|-O "<goal>"[39m, documented in [38;5;153m--help[39m and [38;5;153m--llm[39m. [38;5;153m--orchestrator[39m with an explicit [38;5;153m--copilot[39m/[38;5;153m--agent copilot[39m exits non-zero rather than downgrading (Copilot has
  no [38;5;153m--append-system-prompt[39m equivalent, so the instructions would be dropped).

  [1mTUI[0m — [38;5;153mO[39m in the Sessions view, advertised in the hint bar next to [38;5;153mn new[39m. It reuses the existing repo → worktree-choice → name flow (including scoped repos), skipping only the agent picker
  since the mode is Claude-only, with the branch prompt prefilled [38;5;153morchestrator[39m.

  [1mTests[0m — [38;5;153me2e/orchestrator.spec.ts[39m asserts each required directive is in the prompt; [38;5;153me2e/cli.spec.ts[39m covers the flag, the slug default and [38;5;153m--name[39m override, the Copilot refusal, resume
  re-injection, and the inverse (a plain [38;5;153mlaunch[39m gets no orchestrator text); [38;5;153me2e/launcher.spec.ts[39m drives [38;5;153mO[39m through to the spawned argv, plus the inverse for [38;5;153mn[39m. The CLI launch tests run from a
  repo in the mock home — from [38;5;153mREPO_ROOT[39m the fake git would have [38;5;153mmkdir[39m'd a worktree inside your real repo.

